net "Time series net"
# For a time series of satellite images: 4 bands × 6 dates × 32×32 pixels per sample (input (4, 6, 32, 32)). Two paths from the same
# input: an image path (Conv3D over dates and pixels, then temporal attention per pixel to one image, then 2-D convolutions; U-TAE
# style), and a sequence path (the mean of each date's pixels, then a 1-D convolution, an LSTM, a GRU and a transformer encoder over the
# dates; TSViT style). Both end in one vector each, joined for the output. The tests build it and CI runs it in PyTorch.

1 input
2 conv3d 16 3x3 time 3
3 bn
4 conv3d 16 3x3 time 3 stride 2
5 temporal_pool attention
6 conv 32 3x3
7 maxpool 2x2
8 global_pool

# the sequence path: one vector per date
9 to_sequence <- 1
10 conv1d 16 3
11 lstm 16 bi
12 gru 16
13 cls_pos
14 attention heads 2
15 token_pool cls

16 concat <- 8, 15
17 dense 32
18 output
